<title>JAPAN: Japan end-Feb kerosene stocks up 33 pct yr/yr-MITI.</title>
<headline>Japan end-Feb kerosene stocks up 33 pct yr/yr-MITI.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's kerosene stockpiles stood at 2.5 million kilolitres (kl) as of the end of February, up 33.0 percent from a year earlier, but down 25.7 percent from a month earlier, the Ministry of International Trade and Industry (MITI) said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Demand for kerosene, used for heating, peaks in Japan during the four-month period from November to February.</p>
</text>
